A class that calls Base: without declaring an :INHERIT: every Base:
reference flags (diag.base_requires_inherit). Me: references in the same
methods are fine, and the standalone/outside-class Base codes must not
also fire on the same token.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS ReportWriter;
:DECLARE sTitle;

:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	Base:Constructor();
	Me:sTitle := "Untitled";
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Render;
	:DECLARE sOut;
	sOut := Base:Render();
	:RETURN Me:sTitle + sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS ReportWriter;
:DECLARE sTitle;

:PROCEDURE Constructor;
	Base:Constructor();
	Me:sTitle := "Untitled";
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE Render;
	:DECLARE sOut;
	sOut := Base:Render();
	:RETURN Me:sTitle + sOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:2-5:6 error base_requires_inherit: 'Base:MemberName' requires ':INHERIT' in the current ':CLASS' definition
11:10-11:14 error base_requires_inherit: 'Base:MemberName' requires ':INHERIT' in the current ':CLASS' definition
